From 166cebe0e76d2f6d88cfc6d72483274c471372b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ant=C3=B3nio=20Sarmento?= <Keyaku@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 19:28:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Resolve the ExternalStorageService before a public volume
 mounts

A visible public volume is mounted before the user is unlocked, but the
ExternalStorageService component was only resolved from onUnlockUser. The
mount callback therefore threw "Not ready to bind", vold treated the mount as
failed, and the card was marked unmountable long enough to raise a "Problem
with SD card" notification before a later retry mounted it cleanly.

Resolving the component needs nothing but PackageManager, so do it on demand
when it has not been resolved yet. A failure still leaves the component null
and behaves exactly as before.

Changes:
- `getExternalStorageServiceComponentName` resolves the component lazily instead of returning null while a mount is waiting on it

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I678a05f207290aa8a0fedea226781aaddb7145f9
---
 .../android/server/storage/StorageSessionController.java | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/storage/StorageSessionController.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/storage/StorageSessionController.java
index 0d059ae3..f7f1f747 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/storage/StorageSessionController.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/storage/StorageSessionController.java
@@ -324,6 +324,15 @@ public final class StorageSessionController {
     /** Returns the {@link ExternalStorageService} component name. */
     @Nullable
     public ComponentName getExternalStorageServiceComponentName() {
+        // A visible public volume mounts before onUnlockUser resolves this, and
+        // failing the mount marks the card unmountable. Resolving needs only PM.
+        if (mExternalStorageServiceComponent == null) {
+            try {
+                initExternalStorageServiceComponent();
+            } catch (ExternalStorageServiceException e) {
+                Slog.w(TAG, "Could not resolve the ExternalStorageService yet", e);
+            }
+        }
         return mExternalStorageServiceComponent;
     }
 
